From 17cdf5ae525fcadf3ff41c81b43869dc7496a123 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: b1air <dimazzzzz342@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:01:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add minimize_target: windows shrink into the dock and come
 back out
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A window sent to the scratchpad (`move scratchpad`, or hidden again by
`scratchpad show`) leaves a copy of what it showed, which shrinks into
its minimize_target and fades as it goes; shown again, the window grows
back out of the same place. `minimize_target <x> <y> <w> <h>|none` sets
the place per window, in layout coordinates — the dock sets each
window's to its icon — and without one it is an icon's worth above the
bottom of the window's output, where a dock is.

The copy holds the window's buffers, so the window can close while it
is in flight. Only with animation_duration_ms and a window_animation
other than none. get_tree reports the target as "minimize_target".
